WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:10.990
Please don't expect too much from it.
This story is a simple illustration of the three
Minami sisters and the ordinary life they lead.

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:24.000
All right!

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:58.010
What's Said Here, Stays Here

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.390
Huh?

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.220
Are you sick, Kumada-sensei?

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.020
No, it's just hay fever.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:09.560
It's horrible whenever spring comes around.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:12.480
My nose keeps running,
and my eyes get all teary.

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.110
Hay fever, huh?

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:18.040
It sounds horrible.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:18.780
Yeah.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:26.160
Could this mysterious itch
in my nose be hay fever?

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.710
Maybe these mysterious tears that won't stop streaming down my face are hay fever too.

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:32.480
What's wrong, you two?

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.800
Did something happen?

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.960
Oh, Chiaki.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:37.510
Listen, Chiaki.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.840
We might be suffering from hay fever.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.350
Oh, really? That sounds horrible.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:46.850
Hey, Chiaki! I bet you don't
think it's horrible at all!

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:50.200
No, I just don't think it's worth crying over.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.700
That's right, Chiaki! It's horrible!

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.360
What're you picking your nose for?

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:56.230
It doesn't look horrible at all!

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:00.110
Oh, right.

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:05.030
It's not hay fever, but I think I might have a different kind of allergy.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.290
A different kind of allergy?

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:08.330
Yeah.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:11.460
Whenever I get home,
my body feels heavy,

00:03:11.770 --> 00:03:13.630
my ears start ringing,

00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:16.380
and then I feel tired.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.720
That sounds horrible.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:22.120
No, it's not worth crying over.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.260
Must be horrible for you, Chiaki.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:28.850
I bet you don't think it's as horrible as your boogers, you moron!

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:33.180
I wonder what Chiaki's allergic to.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:36.150
If the symptoms show when she gets home,

00:03:36.830 --> 00:03:41.900
that means the cause of her allergies—
the allergen—is in her home.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:45.910
I know he's trying to be serious, but the nosepicking ruins the whole thing.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:52.420
Uchida, I want to help Chiaki. As a friend.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:57.300
I'd rather not have a friend who
.brazenly picks his nose in public.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.760
I know he was trying to be serious, but...

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:02.930
Right?

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.350
Chiaki, I came over to hang out!

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:09.220
Oh, Mako-chan. Welcome.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.480
I'm back.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.350
Welcome home!

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:17.980
Hey, Chiaki, don't you feel
like going flower viewing?

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:20.230
I told you, they haven't bloomed yet.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:23.150
Then let's go flower bud viewing!

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:25.200
That doesn't count as flower viewing!

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.410
And you're heavy. Get off.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.700
Whenever she gets home,
..her body feels heavy...

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.830
Let's go! Let's go! Let's go flower viewing!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:33.500
Quit screaming it in my ears, you moron!

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.120
Come on! Let's go flower viewing!
Quit screaming it in my ears, you moron!

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.420
Then her ears start ringing...

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:39.340
But they'll wither!

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:40.510
The cherry blossoms'll all wither!

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.130
How can they wither if they haven't even bloomed yet, you moron?!

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:45.090
Let's go see the cherry blossoms!

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.180
Geez. Every single day.
Let's go see the cherry blossoms!

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:48.640
I'm so tired of this.
Let's go see the cherry blossoms!

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:48.680
Let's go see the cherry blossoms!

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.100
And then she feels tired!

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:51.560
Kana-chan!

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.730
You're Chiaki's allergen!

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.060
Kana-chan! Stop being mean to Chiaki!

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:00.730
Did I do something mean
enough to make you cry?

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.860
Stay away from Chiaki, Kana!

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.110
Gross! <i>You</i> stay away from <i>me</i>!

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.110
And you're Mako-chan right now!

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.120
Don't forget that!

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.870
I'll punish allergens like you!

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.250
Stop! Don't point that thing at me!

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:15.870
Use a tissue!

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.750
Why do you want to go
flower viewing so badly?

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.010
I just have a burning desire to
.go flower viewing right now.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.590
Are you all right, Chiaki?

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.510
Yeah, somehow.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:28.390
But...

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:31.720
It's too early to go flower viewing right now.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:33.470
They haven't even bloomed yet.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.560
We can just go again after they've bloomed.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:38.150
Then we can go flower viewing lots of times.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:38.820
Oh.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:38.840
You're right.
Oh.

00:05:38.840 --> 00:05:39.900
You're right.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:40.920
Right?

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.230
Let's go flower viewing!

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:43.030
Yeah!

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.060
Chiaki! Let's go flower viewing!

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.530
Flower viewing! Flower viewing!

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.280
I told you, they haven't bloomed yet.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.780
You morons!

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.540
Flower viewing! Flower viewing! Flower viewing!

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:58.040
What I've got is a moron allergy!
Flower viewing! Flower viewing! Flower viewing!

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:58.390
Flower viewing! Flower viewing! Flower viewing!

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:02.040
A new type of allergen.
And it's spreading.
Flower viewing! Flower viewing! Flower viewing!

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:03.550
Infirmary

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:06.800
Is there a cure for moronicity?

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:08.300
Nope!

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.180
Yeah, thought so.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.440
Timing is really important.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:19.520
What are you talking about?

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.940
Flower viewing, I think.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.820
If you're too early, no one'll come,

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.740
but if you're too late, the season'll be over.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.360
Flower viewing is all about timing.

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:46.050
Fujioka-kun had some great timing there.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.800
Really great! He's on the soccer team, after all!

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:50.470
What was great about it?

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:54.100
If my foot smells like milk forever, and I can't be a bride,

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.930
Fujioka's taking responsibility!

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.310
Responsibility?!

00:06:59.020 --> 00:07:01.270
Take responsibility!

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.270
I'll take it!

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.110
Invite me to the ceremony, 'kay?

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:09.700
You're the matchmaker, Miyuki-chan.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:11.660
W-W-W-Wait, Kana!

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.160
Nah, just kidding.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.330
Kidding?!

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:17.370
His habit of kicking everything
is pretty problematic.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.370
Habit?

00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:23.210
Fujioka wants to kick everything in his way so bad, he just can't help it.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:24.960
He's the ball-kicking Badass.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:29.090
No, it was just a coincidence
.that he kicked it when it fell.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:31.430
Then let's give him a test.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.590
A test?

00:07:32.590 --> 00:07:34.100
One with a kind-of-bad score?

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:36.470
There.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:41.020
Hey, Kana, you should put
.your trash in the trash can.

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:44.020
No, you need to take that home with you!

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:46.610
Minami, I got some slippers.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:54.200
Huh? Did I kick something just now?

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.040
Keiko, I'm borrowing your eraser.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:06.670
All right. Time for the next test.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:23.640
Couldn't you at least use your own eraser?

00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:27.400
And now, the ball.

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.780
If he kicks this one, it's a hat trick.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:31.650
D-Don't you think we should call it quits?

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.650
And there.

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.340
Handball!

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.880
All right! The final test!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:49.560
A rag?

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.300
What are you going to do with that?

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.640
We'll put it somewhere Fujioka'll walk and see if he kicks it or slips on it.

00:08:55.640 --> 00:08:57.970
Which'll it be? Which'll it be?

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:00.890
I'll put it right here...

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:02.930
and wait.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.060
That's dangerous. Stop it.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:14.740
I'm sorry.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:17.990
Kana, can't you just forgive him?

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.370
No, I can't!

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:23.330
Thanks to Fujioka, I'm
wearing something weird!

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:26.420
Now I can't be a bride!

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:30.420
Can't you just put on a tracksuit top too?

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:31.750
Oh, you're right.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.340
Th-That's not true!

00:09:34.930 --> 00:09:38.590
Even if you can't be a bride, I'll...

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:43.680
I'll... Minami, I'll...

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:46.190
Fujioka?

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.480
Oh that Kana, leaving the ball right—

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.240
Minami, I'll take—

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:55.490
Huh?

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.830
U-Um... Minami?

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:07.330
Nice shot.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:11.920
You think I'd say that?!

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.280
You damn ball-kicking Badass!

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:30.400
Something tasty?

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:33.820
I'm sorry, all I have right now is juice...

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.320
No, not right now.

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.990
I was just wondering what was in season.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:43.530
Oh, I think fava beans
.are in season right now.

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:45.370
Fava beans?

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.540
Now we're talking!

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:49.750
I'd love to try some boiled
in their pods in salt water!

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.460
That sounds great.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.130
And maybe even sit under a cherry
..blossom tree in full bloom and...

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:02.260
Huh? What are you drinking?

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.350
Gimme 'nother pint!

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.020
Hosaka, Hosaka.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:09.310
Don't bother me, Hayami.

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:10.300
Death!

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:13.020
That hurt.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.940
What do you mean, bother you?

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:18.240
I was going to share something nice with you too.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.300
Something nice?

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:20.860
You wanna hear it?

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:21.960
I'm not interested.

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:22.820
I see.

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:23.370
Guess that's it.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:27.620
I'm not interested, but I have no objections to hearing it.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.480
Fava beans.

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:32.250
That is the only answer.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.250
Fava... beans?

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:43.760
All right. That should be everything.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:48.770
Haruka-neesama said I could
.buy any one thing I wanted.

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.100
What should I get?

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:55.150
Some chocolate would be nice,
.but some chips would be good too.

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.360
A new soda would be—

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.440
Fava beans.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:02.400
The Curry Fairy!

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:05.200
No, wait, is he the Vegetable Fairy today?

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.200
Fava beans.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:07.280
<b>Fava
Beans
Fava beans.</b>

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:07.330
Fava beans are the only answer.
<b>Fava
Beans</b>

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:10.040
<b>Fava
Beans
Fava beans are the only answer.</b>

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.960
Fava beans are the answer?

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:15.540
Then what about chocolate or chips?

00:12:16.070 --> 00:12:18.300
Fava beans work in all sorts of dishes.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.510
They go in stir-fries.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:23.180
And they're great in soups.

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.220
You can even put them in croquettes and other fried foods.

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:30.020
Not to mention fava bean rice.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:31.560
The main dish!

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:33.020
Yes! A pasta!

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.060
Spring cabbage.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:41.110
A pasta with fava beans,
cabbage, and peperoncini!

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.570
It's the perfect seasonal meal.

00:12:45.070 --> 00:12:48.080
All I need now is garlic and pepper flakes.

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.580
Speaking of which...

00:12:50.580 --> 00:12:53.800
We got a very good cabbage today.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:56.460
I'll get some fava beans!

00:12:57.010 --> 00:13:00.210
Huh? Chiaki-chan bought fava beans yesterday?

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:01.670
Yes!

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:06.680
She usually buys something sugary, but I guess she's starting to like vegetables!

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:07.680
Oh?

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:09.470
I wonder what happened.

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:13.980
She said she just had to have a pasta with fava beans, cabbage, and peperoncini!

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:16.270
That sounds great!

00:13:16.270 --> 00:13:18.480
And maybe some garlic
and pepper flakes to taste!

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:25.570
What are you drinking?

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.240
So, where's my share?

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.780
What?!

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:33.000
Minami Haruka has already had a pasta
with fava beans, cabbage, and peperoncini?

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:41.000
Then I won't be able to excite her with the novelty of this fava bean, cabbage, and peperoncini pasta lunch.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.760
You made the same thing?

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:45.260
How could this happen?

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:48.340
The season for fava beans has passed.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:52.390
I guess the season for cherry blossoms is next.

00:13:53.390 --> 00:13:55.020
Cherry blossoms?

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:56.270
Sounds good.

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:02.270
What are you drinking?

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:05.820
It looks like Chiaki likes vegetables now, so...

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:09.280
All right! Maybe I'll make a stir-fry full of carrots tonight!

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:11.080
Please, spare her.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.080
Carrots are scary!

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.500
Bell peppers are scary!

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:16.710
Huh?

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:22.780
I want to go flower viewing.

00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:24.050
But...

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:27.010
Aren't the parks crowded at this time of year?

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:29.180
We won't have anywhere to sit.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.390
Should we go?

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:31.900
I dunno if we can...

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:32.430
Yeah...

00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:35.680
I'm going to go practice soccer with Fujioka.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.940
Sorry. I've got hay fever.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:42.230
No one took me up on
.my invitation in the end.

00:14:42.230 --> 00:14:44.480
I found such a good place,

00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:46.940
but nobody wants to come
.if I invite them directly.

00:14:48.450 --> 00:14:50.740
Hey, this is just between us, but...

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:53.740
What is it, Uchida?

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:58.440
Touma went into the boys' bathroom by mistake the other day!

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:00.780
Why'd you tell them?!

00:15:00.780 --> 00:15:04.200
I told you, that was just between us!

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.300
Really?

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.760
You should be more careful, Uchida.

00:15:07.760 --> 00:15:10.180
Normal people don't go
.into the wrong bathroom.

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:10.840
No way!

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:11.800
Everyone does it sometimes!

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:13.180
Like about twice a year.

00:15:13.180 --> 00:15:15.010
That's pretty often.

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:15.810
Yeah.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:18.930
Then what's average?
About once a year?

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.940
The average person doesn't even
.mess up once in their <i>life</i>, you moron.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.480
Really?

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.650
Don't forget to check which
.one it is before you go in.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.990
Oh, right, don't they have toilets that look like waterfalls in boys' bathrooms?

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:31.110
Huh? What're those?

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:33.400
Sounds like you know a lot about them. Have you seen them before?

00:15:33.400 --> 00:15:33.950
I-I don't know a lot about them!

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:36.240
This is getting kind of heated.
I-I don't know a lot about them!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:39.750
Touma's the one who peeked inside the boys' bathroom!

00:15:39.750 --> 00:15:42.840
I didn't peek! I just walked in by mistake!

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:45.120
Normal people don't walk in by mistake!

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:46.500
They totally do!

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:48.050
You know what I mean, right, Chiaki?

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:54.390
Don't spin your questions to make it sound like <i>I</i> was the one who went into the boys' bathroom by mistake.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:55.720
What'd you say?!

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.310
Go easy on me! We're fellow Minamis, aren't we?

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:01.520
Yeah, we're fellow Minamis! That's why I don't want you to mess up!

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:03.650
What about you, Kana-chan?

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.610
Huh? What?

00:16:05.610 --> 00:16:09.070
How many times a year do you mix up the boys' and girls' bathrooms?

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:10.570
Me?

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:13.700
Back when I was in fifth grade,
I went in the wrong one three times.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:16.240
Huh? No way, that many times?

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.740
Three times?

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:19.080
That's way too much.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.960
I never thought you guys'd
..get creeped out by it...

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.250
This is just between us, but...

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.040
Huh?

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:29.580
Riko-chan's really good at knitting.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.760
Hey, wait!

00:16:31.070 --> 00:16:34.840
You knitted a scarf for the guy you like, but you never gave it to him.

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.140
No! No!

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:40.810
Really? But you said it was just between us and told me that.

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:44.560
If something's just between us,
it's supposed to <i>stay</i> between us!

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:46.610
What did I do wrong?

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:47.650
Um...

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:52.030
When you say "just between us," it means that it's just between the people there at the time.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:54.070
You can't tell anyone else.

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:55.320
Huh? Huh?

00:16:55.650 --> 00:16:57.490
It means it's a secret.

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:00.490
I'm sorry, Riko-chan!

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.250
Yeah, that's right!

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.920
I've never been able to leverage my skills!

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:08.250
Hey, hey, hey!

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.250
This is just between us, but...

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.210
Huh?

00:17:11.210 --> 00:17:14.380
Atsuko's boobs gained a level!

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:15.840
W-Wait, Maki!

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:17.930
Ehh? Let's see! Let's see!

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:19.350
Not you too, Haruka!

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.850
Me too! Let's see!

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:29.440
They did gain a level.

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:30.940
Right, right?

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:33.070
What've you been eating?

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:37.320
I said it was just between us,
but now everyone knows!

00:17:37.630 --> 00:17:39.660
Maki!

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:40.830
Sorry, sorry.

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.580
But when someone says it's "just between us," you feel like telling other people.

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.840
What's wrong, Kana-chan?

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:54.170
Maki-chan, I'm counting on you to keep this just between us!

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:58.800
Let's hear it.

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:06.140
This is just between us, but there's a great flower viewing spot on the hill on the other side of town.

00:18:06.650 --> 00:18:11.000
It's a secret place, so you can't tell anyone.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:14.080
And next Sunday'll be the best time to go viewing there.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:15.690
Got it?

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:18.030
It's just between us.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.620
Hosaka, Hosaka.

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:26.580
What?

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.710
This is just between us, but...

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:30.290
Just between us?

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.420
Actually, no, never mind.

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:36.630
This is just between us, but...

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:39.130
...or so I heard!

00:18:42.810 --> 00:18:44.350
Oh, really?

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:49.640
I can't wait for Sunday!

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:36.020
Guess I was a bit too early, even counting the time it took to get snacks together.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.750
Fine! I'll just start without them!

00:19:52.050 --> 00:19:53.670
Cheers!

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:58.510
I'll wait just a little longer.

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:08.060
This is just between us,

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:11.220
but I shouldn't have kept it just between us.

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:15.480
What are you doing?

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:19.780
Sorry. It took longer than
.we expected to make lunch.

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:20.820
Geez.

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:24.700
If you knew a good place like this,
you should've told us sooner, you moron.

00:20:28.070 --> 00:20:29.410
What took you so long?

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.750
The flower viewing season will
be long gone at this rate!

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.380
Wh-What is it?

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:38.380
Let's watch those flowers together, Kana.

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:39.880
Can I sit here?

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.470
Hurry up and sit down!

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.760
It's time for some flower viewing!

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:47.180
All right, we ready?

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:48.180
Yeah!

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:49.180
Yeah.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:51.060
One, two...

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:53.310
Cheers!

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:55.440
All right, let's eat!

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.360
Don't hold back either, Chiaki!

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.320
But, Haruka! Don't you think
this is way too much?

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.690
It'll be tough for the three
of us to finish alone.

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:03.030
I think we'll be fine.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:03.700
Yeah.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:05.070
It's about time.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:05.950
See?

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:15.000
This is just between us, but your "just between us" tactic is pretty good.

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:18.210
This is just between us, but thanks, Kana.

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:20.710
I see. You're a teacher at Touma's school?

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:24.170
Yes. Touma-kun's very smart and very athletic!

00:21:24.170 --> 00:21:24.800
I wonder what she teaches.
Yes. Touma-kun's very smart and very athletic!

00:21:24.800 --> 00:21:26.720
It's a joy having her!
I wonder what she teaches.

00:21:27.210 --> 00:21:29.510
Oh, so you're good with charcoal too?

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:30.100
Yeah.

00:21:30.430 --> 00:21:33.140
I'm a bit of an outdoors guy myself.

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:34.680
When I barbecue meat, it's like—

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.730
I'm going to start by grilling the vegetables.

00:21:36.730 --> 00:21:37.850
Oh, sorry.

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:40.440
It's a barbecue, Yoshino!

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:42.480
It's a barbecue, Uchida.

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:44.900
Man, elementary schoolers are so innocent, they're cute.

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:46.950
Yay! It's a barbecue!

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:48.870
Middle schoolers are innocent too.

00:21:49.310 --> 00:21:50.700
Let's go, Touma!

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:52.370
Bring it, Fujioka!

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:55.320
Makoto, Shuuichi, we're going up against a middle schooler.

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:56.620
Don't hold back!

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:57.830
Leave it to me!

00:21:57.830 --> 00:22:01.630
The burning soul of the fantasista
within me can never be extinguished!

00:22:01.630 --> 00:22:04.800
Makoto, do you even know
what "fantasista" means?

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:05.630
Nope!

00:22:09.700 --> 00:22:14.560
Fujioka-kun's having so much fun with a
...middle school girl I've never seen before...

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:16.480
Wait, is that a boy?

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:18.400
Why don't you join them, Riko?

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:20.230
We're going all out today!

00:22:20.230 --> 00:22:21.730
You can't drink that.

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:23.860
Why? It's just fizzy wheat juice.

00:22:23.860 --> 00:22:26.030
But it's not juice, is it?

00:22:26.030 --> 00:22:26.990
Yeah.

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:28.070
Then you can't drink it!

00:22:41.010 --> 00:22:42.460
Minami Haruka.

00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:45.700
Are you viewing the cherry blossoms somewhere today too?

00:22:45.700 --> 00:22:46.800
Yes, very good.

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:50.970
Enjoy the changing of the seasons with those close to you.

00:22:51.390 --> 00:22:54.100
That is the joy of life!

00:22:54.490 --> 00:22:57.600
Now, let us enjoy the coming of spring!

00:23:11.650 --> 00:23:13.700
Kana, your ribbon's coming undone.

00:23:13.700 --> 00:23:14.830
Oh, you're right.

00:23:14.830 --> 00:23:16.240
Come on, come here.

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:18.750
I was in a rush.

00:23:19.050 --> 00:23:22.250
Geez. You should've just woken up earlier.

00:23:22.250 --> 00:23:24.790
But you want to sleep as long as you can in the morning!

00:23:25.210 --> 00:23:26.800
There, all tied.

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:29.010
Now, shall we go?

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:30.430
Okay!

00:23:32.340 --> 00:23:35.010
See you later!
